    "Dry Bulk Freight": "Capesize: The Capesize C5TC average improved by USD 7.1k/day closing the week at USD 44,896/ day. Trip from Continent to F.East is up by 6.2k/ day at USD 80,417/day, Transatlantic R/V is higher by 10k/day at USD 50,188/day, and Bolivar to Rotterdam is higher by 10.7k/day at USD 56,458/ day, while Transpacific R/V is increased by 8.5k/ day at USD 50,209/day. Trip from Tubarao to Rotterdam is increased by 7.4k/day at USD 35,990/day, China-Brazil R/V is higher by 5.9k/day at USD 45,858/day, and & trip from Saldanha Bay to Qinqdao is increased by 7.4k/day at USD 35,990/day.\n\nKamsarmax/Panamax: The Kamsarmax P5TC Timecharter average started the week at USD 18,928/day closing with an increase at USD 20,834/day. Trip from Skaw-Gib to F.East is im- proved by 1.6k/day at USD 30,339/day, Pacific R/ Vis up by 2.4k/day at USD 19,300/day, while Transatlantic R/V is increased by 2k/day at USD 20,541/day, and Singapore R/V via Atlantic is in- creased by 1.9k/day at USD 22,033/day.\n\nUltramax/Supramax: The Ultramax S11TC average closed the week at USD 20,819/day. The Supramax S10TC average closed the week about 0.1k/day higher than its opening at USD 18,785/day. The Bal- tic Supramax Asia S3TC average closed the week about 0.5k/day higher than previous week at USD 19,150/day. N.China one Australian or Pacific R/V is improved by 0.5k/day at USD 18,981/day, USG to Skaw Passero is firmer by 0.6k/day at USD 30,472/ day. S.China trip via Indonesia to EC India is up by 0.6k/day at USD 22,682/day, trip from S.China via Indonesia to S.China pays USD 15,863/day, while Med/B.Sea to China/S.Korea is reduced by 0.9k/day at USD 23,371/day.\n\nHandysize: The Handysize HS7TC average closed the week improved by 0.1k/day at USD 15,855/day. Skaw-Passero trip to Boston-Galveston pays 0.3k/ day more at USD 10,721/day, Brazil to Cont. pays 1.2k/day more at USD 22,494/day, S.E. Asia trip to Spore/Japan 0.2k/day is firmer at USD 18,081/day, China/S.Korea/Japan round trip is reduced by0.1k/ day at USD 17,225/day, and trip from U.S. Gulf to Cont. is reduced by 0.7k/day at USD 14,964/day, while N.China-S.Korea-Japan trip to S.E.Asia is in- creased by 0.2k/day at USD 17,725/day.",
